<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngbanya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ngbanya are the ruling estate of Gonja in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, descendants of the Mande horsemen who conquered the region under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndewura-jakpa">Ndewura Jakpa</a> in the 17th century. They hold the chieftaincies of Gonja's divisions, while Muslim scholars and the older commoner peoples form the other estates of Gonja society.</p></div>
